Hundreds have reportedly been killed on Nias off the Sumatra coast.
In 2006, a magnitude 6.8 quake struck Indonesia's most-populated Java island, triggering a tsunami hitting the south coast, killing close to 700 people.
In 2009, an earthquake of magnitude 7.6 hit the western Suma-tra-provinced province of Paddang.
More than 1,100 people were killed.
In 2010, a magnitude 7.5 quake struck one of Sumatra's Mentawai Islands, triggering a 10-meter-long tsunami that destroyed dozens of villages and killed about 300 people.
